{#- The Renovate agent's caps and permission mode: config.env.j2, homelab-renovate-agent.service.j2
and prompt.txt.j2 import these as `pins`. A template's own assignment outranks every inventory
value, so a PR that edits only host_vars cannot raise a run's PR count, spend or wall clock, or
widen its permission mode. The host package renderer puts the inventory above a component's
defaults, so a component default would pin nothing. This file is on the lander's approval list.
Each value is a literal. hosts/tests/test_renovate_agent_unit.py holds them equal to the
component's defaults/main.yml, which the docs fragments read.
-#}
{%- set max_prs = 3 -%}
{%- set model = "opus" -%}
{%- set permission_mode = "auto" -%}
{%- set budget_usd = 25 -%}
{#- The whole run: the session, then the landings it nominated, one after another. -#}
{%- set run_timeout_s = 67260 -%}
{#- The session alone, which only triages and writes requests. An assumption, not a measurement
of a session that does no landing: the 15 runs to 2026-11-12, landings included, each ended
within 16 minutes of the timer. It and one whole landing fit inside run_timeout_s. -#}
{%- set session_timeout_s = 2700 -%}
{%- set unit_timeout = "1131min" -%}
